So, I have a couple of questions about lu ... li'u that I haven't found in
the CLL yet.

A: lo gerku goi ko'a cu barda
B: .i la saimon cusku lu ko'a cu xunre li'u

Now, does the {ko'a} in the quote that B is referring to refer to "lo gerku"
or potentially something else entirely?  Or does the presence of a {ko'a}
without a {goi} assignment within that quote make the entire quote
ungrammatical.

Furthermore, if we have:

A: la saimon cusku lu mi barda li'u

is "mi" saimon or the speaker "A"?

- Luke Bergen

